Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:14:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] SYCL Inkling fusions on ggml-org master: control()
 gates fused after the down mat-vec (bit 512), Q8_0 weights in relmask

master builds control() as CONCAT(rms(cur), rms(msg)) and SUB(cur, forget*cur); the old matcher never fired.
The new one starts at the forget MUL_MAT (the regular mat-vec computes h) and runs the 8 gate nodes as one
kernel. Q8_0 weights (AoS or reordered planar) read through wmat_at/_at4, also for the relmask sink projection
(AtomicChat AD-Q4_K stores attn_sink_proj as Q8_0). GGML_SYCL_IFUSE default 1023 (decimal).
AD-Q4_K: tg64 57.6 -> 61.2, pp512 936 -> 1157.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: otaliptus <56600661+otaliptus@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-sycl/inkling-fuse.cpp | 165 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 159 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

